    "title": "Positive news on Warriors' Steph Curry ahead of team update this week",
    "text": "DENVER — An official update on Stephen Curry’s status for the Golden State Warriors is expected this week, but head coach Steve Kerr gave an unofficial update Sunday before they played the Denver Nuggets. “Doing well,” he said pregame at Ball Arena.  Kerr said he received a text message Sunday from vice president of player health and performance Rick Celebrini, who notified him the injured guard had a “good session” of rehabilitation. Curry, who last played Jan. 30, missed his 25th consecutive game Sunday with right kneecap soreness known as runner’s knee. The next step toward a return to play is a successful scrimmage, and Kerr was mum on whether he was trending toward one, deferring toward the team-issued update upon the team’s return to the Bay Area. Golden State next plays Wednesday at Chase Center against the San Antonio Spurs, followed Thursday with a back-to-back matchup against the Cleveland Cavaliers. Moody update: Moses Moody took to X to issue his first public comments since he ruptured his left patellar tendon. “I appreciate all of the love. Every challenge I’ve been through in life I’m glad I went through. I’m sure I’ll feel the same about this,” the fifth-year swingman wrote on X with a flexing emoji and a picture of him shooting. Moody sustained the season-ending tear last Monday against the Dallas Mavericks and underwent successful surgery Friday in Los Angeles, the team announced. In 60 games this year, Moody delivered career-best averages in scoring (12.1 points per game), rebounding (3.3), assists (1.6) and 3-point shooting (40.1%) while serving as Golden State’s top perimeter defender.",
